            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Lei YU",
                        "email": "mine260309@gmail.com",
                        "username": "mine260309"
                    },
                    "message": "This resolve the issue when call() is used with asio, but be noted that sdbusplus::match has the same issue, and it's resolved by https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/sdbusplus/+/68860, which is not merged."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Willy Tu",
                        "email": "wltu@google.com",
                        "username": "wltu"
                    },
                    "message": "yeah, ideally we have something like in run\n\n```\nwhile (true)\n    {\n        // Block for one job\n        io->run_one();\n\n        // Process all ongoing jobs\n        while (io->poll_one())\n        {\n        }\n\n        // Process all existing dbus messages\n        while (systemBusPtr->process_discard())\n        {\n        }\n    }\n```\n\nto just process any of the read messages so that doesn't get signal anymore. Not sure how to set that up in the sbudplus level.\n\n\ud83d\ude1e"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there an example of using this that would be a correct usage?  Unless we have some example, I'd rather just make sure it's not callable so people aren't surprised."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/asio/connection.hpp",
                    "line": 90,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "1.  Should mark this override?\n\n2. Should we make this no-op instead of trying to fix it?  Is there a correct usage of a sync API in an async reactor?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/asio/connection.hpp",
                    "line": 95,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm still not sure this is correct.  It might make this call not deadlock, but will (likely) cause other async messages to be dropped, or attempted to be handled in the callbacks elsewhere which is definitely not the intent of this.\n\nWe'd need to cancel BEFORE we start the sync call, queue up all callback responses while the sync call was happening, then unload them.\n\n\nAlso, wouldn't we want to cancel BEFORE we do the sync call?  Otherwise we might end up with duplicated reads?"
                }
            ],
